  "headline": "Calibration reduces the growth in confidence error from the simplest to most detailed policy under the binary reward in both models, relative to recipe A. A shared benefit relative to SFT is not established.",
  "interpretation": [
    "Confidence error compares stated confidence with Jaccard rule-set correctness among valid answers; this is distinct from better predictions or confidence ranking.",
    "For Qwen3.5-9B, binary B still worsens from L0 through L1 to L2, but less than A. GPT-OSS-120B binary B improves sharply at L1 and rises slightly at L2. Neither pattern justifies claiming monotonically improving policy following.",
    "The new SFT320 comparisons use each trained arm's full eligible seed roster and one shared baseline. The B-A trend table uses the paired A/B roster. These populations are labeled separately.",
    "Qwen SFT has22,21,18 valid answers at L0,L1,L2; GPT SFT has28,27,28. Conditional common-valid all-level point checks preserve the binary B-A ECE trend direction, but do not replace the full-panel tests.",
    "No shared corrected improvement in F1, Jaccard correctness, ranking, review usefulness, or evidence trend relative to SFT is established. Unavailable tests are retained in multiplicity correction, not interpreted as measured null effects."
  ],
  "scope": "The same28 positive SafePyramid conversations, four in each of seven domains, three native policy levels, one thinking-on answer at each frozen checkpoint/level. Availability-selected secondary study."
